*spoiler warning*

The only animals you can tame without magical means are domestic 
animals, these include horses (pony, horse, warhorse), dogs (little dog, 
dog, large dog) and cats (kitten, housecat, large cat).
The way to tame them is by throwing food to them, but only food they 
like to eat of course. Horses are herbivores, cats and dogs are 
carnivores. For the carnivores, any 'meaty', fresh, non-tainted corpse 
will do, so it's normally very easy to find something (and you already 
keep a bunch od lizard corpses on you perhaps?). They also gladly eat 
most 'people food', rations, candy bars, pancakes, etc - not fruit and 
tins of course. For the herbivores it's much less to choose from, 
basically 'vegan corpses' (lichen), and fruit.
If you happen upon a non-peaceful domestic animal that poses a threat to 
you, and you don't have the proper food to tame it, you can throw other 
food at it, and it will at least become peaceful. Saves you from the 
imminent danger, and you can return later with proper food if you want 
to tame it. The food is not consumed in the process.

Then there are many magical means to tame creatures, and ways to turn 
your already tame creatures into other, hopefully more useful, 
creatures. But perhaps this was enough spoiling for one day?
